/-!
# Uniform polynomial approximation from two transverse graph foliations

Source: Journé, *A Regularity Lemma for Functions of Several Variables* (1988),
pp. 187–193. The arbitrary-positive-block-dimensional proof is the honest agent
expansion of `analysis.journe_transverse_leaf_polynomial_approximation`, with
parent `zhang.rank_one_ambient_g3_journe_regularity`. The scalar printed proof
does not constitute a published proof of this whole weak arbitrary-block variant.

The two atlases below are independent foliation atlases. No common smooth
transverse coordinates or continuous higher leaf jets are imposed. Higher jets
are spatially continuous on each plaque and uniformly bounded across plaques.
Actual overlap changes preserve leaf slices locally, which is the unbranched
foliation condition, rather than a family of unrelated or branching graphs.
-/

noncomputable section

