/-- The exact conclusion in original coordinates, identical to Campanato's approximation input.
No boundary regularity of Ω, measurability replacement, or exponent loss is built in. -/
def HasUniformPolynomialApproximation {N : ℕ} (n : ℕ) (α : ℝ)
    (h : Block N → ℝ) (Ω : Set (Block N)) : Prop :=
  ∀ a₀ ∈ Ω, ∃ V : Set (Block N), IsOpen V ∧ a₀ ∈ V ∧
    ∃ C : ℝ, 0 < C ∧ ∃ r : ℝ, 0 < r ∧
      ∀ a ∈ V, ∃ P : MvPolynomial (Fin N) ℝ,
        P.totalDegree ≤ n ∧ Metric.ball a r ⊆ Ω ∧
          ∀ y ∈ Metric.ball a r,
            |h y - MvPolynomial.eval (fun i ↦ y i) P| ≤ C * ‖y - a‖ ^ ((n : ℝ) + α)

/-- Uniform original-coordinate degree-n polynomial approximation in all positive block dimensions.

Source/provenance: Journé (1988), pp.187–193; the current DAG node is an AGENT expansion
of the omitted higher-dimensional argument, parent zhang.rank_one_ambient_g3_journe_regularity.
The graph-atlas hypotheses are the actual locally common-radius, jointly C1 leaf-graph
premises. Only finite spatial C^{n,α} bounds are imposed, not joint higher jets.
The function outside Ω and the total graph maps outside their specified balls are irrelevant.
Empty Ω is vacuous; no domain boundary assumptions or connectedness are imposed.

